<body>
<div class="rxc-shell top" role="banner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12"/></svg>RadicalxChange</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="here">Mackellar on migration</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="right">
      <span class="status"><i></i><span data-k="status">Preliminary results, data to 12:35pm AEDT, 20 November 2026</span></span>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Mackellar%20migration%20results">Contact the team</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1><span class="ln">Mackellar wants</span><span class="ln"><span class="box">an end to visa limbo</span></span></h1>
        <p class="sub intro" data-k="intro">Multiculturalism is central to Australia’s story, identity and future. As debate over migration levels and settings continues, this process offers a more nuanced, participatory way for communities to give feedback on immigration policy.</p>
        <p class="sub" data-k="herosub">People disagree about how many should come, and how much to do for refugees. But all three groups want visa decisions made in reasonable time, so no one is left in limbo for years. When people voted on priorities, planning migration with housing and infrastructure came first.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Mackellar said</a><a class="btn line" href="#priorities">The changes people want most</a></div>
        <p class="turnout" data-k="turnout">Since 30 October 2026 · 77 people have taken part · 70 in a group</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="glabels" role="list" aria-label="The three groups">
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-1" style="--gc:var(--g1)"><small data-k="hl1n">Group 1 · 20 people</small><b><span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="1">Migration keeps us going; keep families together.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-2" style="--gc:var(--g2)"><small data-k="hl2n">Group 2 · 31 people</small><b><span data-gname="2">Works, if housing keeps up</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="2">Welcome refugees, but match numbers to housing.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-3" style="--gc:var(--g3)"><small data-k="hl3n">Group 3 · 19 people</small><b><span data-gname="3">Fewer, but flexible</span></b><em><span data-gdesc="3">Too many, too quickly; raise the bar for skilled visas.</span></em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <a class="sticker" href="#agree" aria-label="More than 9 in 10 in all three groups say people deserve a visa answer sooner than years after applying. See what they agree on."><div aria-hidden="true" data-k="sticker"><span>More than</span><b>9 in 10</b><span>in all three groups say people deserve a visa answer sooner than years after applying</span></div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Most people fit into one of three groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person, placed by how they voted. People who voted alike sit close together, so the higher the pile, the more people voted that way.</p>
      <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 1000 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-desc"><desc id="map-desc">70 people placed along the main divide in the votes. Group 1, Migration works, 20 people, sits to the left. Group 2, Works, if housing keeps up, 31 people, the largest group, sits in the middle and overlaps Group 1. Group 3, Fewer, but flexible, 19 people, is spread out to the right.</desc></svg>
      <div class="map-foot">
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint"><span class="h-fine">Hover over a dot to see how that person voted.</span><span class="h-touch">Tap the map or press “Show me someone” to see how one person voted.</span></p>
    </div>
    <!-- "Where would you sit?" (piloted on the Curtin page) goes here, under the map, once it is a shared block. -->

    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one" id="group-1">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g1f">3<small> in </small>10</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g1"></i><span>Group 1: <span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></span></b><span data-k="g1n">20 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols" data-k="card1">
          <div class="qbox"><q>Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>95%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>63%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>35%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(17 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Migration is about people, not just workers. Families being able to live together should count as much as economic contribution.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>95%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>68%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>39%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Migration at current levels have negligble impacts (&lt;1%) upon housing prices and rents in metropolitan areas</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>85%</b> of Group 1 agree <span class="nn">(13 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>60%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>17%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(12 voted)</span></span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two" id="group-2">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g2f"><small class="mt">More than </small>2<small> in </small>5</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g2"></i><span>Group 2: <span data-gname="2">Works, if housing keeps up</span></span></b><span data-k="g2n">31 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">Where they stand</p>
        <div class="gcols two" data-k="card2">
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g1"></i><span>Like Group 1 · <span data-gname="1">Migration works</span></span></p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>So long as Australia supports wars in foreign countries we have a duty to support the refugees from those wars</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>88%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>93%</b> of Group 1 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>7%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren't so lucky, even when it costs us.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>85%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>22%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g3"></i><span>Like Group 3 · <span data-gname="3">Fewer, but flexible</span></span></p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Partner and family visas should have reasonable limits on the number of eligible family members included.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>90%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>29%</b> of Group 1 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>92%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(13 voted)</span></span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Federal and state governments must agree on annual migration numbers based on housing, infrastructure and public service capacity.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>90%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>29%</b> of Group 1 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>83%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(12 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="gcol wide"><p class="side">More than both other groups</p>
            <div class="qbox wide"><q>immigration needs to be linked to net new housing.  It seems counterintuitive to let more people in than we can house</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>81%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>21%</b> of Group 1 <span class="nn">(14 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>42%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(12 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard three" id="group-3">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g3f">1<small> in </small>4</span><span class="who"><b><i class="dot g3"></i><span>Group 3: <span data-gname="3">Fewer, but flexible</span></span></b><span data-k="g3n">19 people</span></span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols" data-k="card3">
          <div class="qbox"><q>People who choose to come here should be expected to cover more of the cost of settling in, including learning English.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>79%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(19 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>10%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>34%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>72%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>0%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>29%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Raising the bar for skilled visas would bring in people who contribute more, even if it means fewer of them overall.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>83%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>0%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>44%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note" data-k="caveat">The people who joined in aren’t a random sample, so these groups describe who took part, not all of Mackellar. 7 people voted on too few statements to be placed in a group.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block deep" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head side">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
      <p class="head-line" data-k="agreelead">At least 7 in 10 people in every group agreed with 31 statements. Here are five of them, each beside a related statement the groups disagree on.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
    <details class="all">
      <summary data-k="foldsum">See all 31 statements all three groups agreed with</summary>
      <ol class="all-list" id="all"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap" data-k="qvcap">At a community session on 19 November, 39 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding" data-k="finding">In the conversation, most people in every group agreed with four of the top six.</p>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t" data-k="no-t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s" data-k="no-s">18 people opposed it and 12 backed it.</p></div>
